From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tyn <tyn@localhost>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 06:02:34 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] tyn: sg-pc save / load layout from the original Game.exe,
 configurable save grid

Replaces estimated values of patch 0022 with the layout the original STEINS;GATE (Steam) Game.exe draws (save menu
draw routine around 0x43b661, drawSprite 0x432230; the game works in 1280x720 units and draws at x1.5):
- 8 slots per page in 2 columns x 4 rows (0022 guessed 6). 1280-space loop x0 = 86 (+579), y0 = 162 (+127); the
  slot card is the sheet's own (1921.5, 1.5, 789 x 166.5) drawn at ((x0 - 10) * 1.5, (y0 - 75) * 1.5), i.e.
  x 114 / 982.5, y 130.5 / 321 / 511.5 / 702 (0022 took that card for a banner and drew an invisible patch).
- Thumbnail 240 x 135 at card + (15, 15); "NO DATA" is the sheet's (2713.5, 1.5, 240 x 135).
- 48 slots / 8 = 6 pages, which is also the "/6" page art of the sheets.

Generic (MO6TWPC save menu): the grid size is read from the optional profile fields EntriesPerRow / RowsPerPage
(defaults 2 x 3, the Memories Off 6 PC layout, so that profile is unchanged); the page count follows from it.

Not yet from the original: the slot texts (the original draws "No." + two digits at card + (180, 13) * 1.5, the
scene title lines from a text table at (416, 13) / (180, 41) and more at (258, 73) in 1280 units), the lock icon
and the 85 x 36 page tabs at y 934; those still use the 0022 estimates.

Checked on MuMu: sg-pc load screen shows 8 original cards with thumbnails and "1 / 6", loading slot 4 works;
mo6tw-pc-zhs load screen unchanged (2 x 3, "1 / 8").

diff --git a/profiles/sg-pc/hud/savemenu.lua b/profiles/sg-pc/hud/savemenu.lua
